{"date": "2026-11-11", "word": "Light", "summary": "A light day (forecast moderate). Thermals were strongest (moderate) about 15:00. The upslope ran from about 09:00 to about 17:00. A high day for November: the base reached about 5,600 ft (normal 4,500\u20135,500 ft). The evening before, the page called it normal, about 5,200 ft, a miss. Midday the base averaged about 5,600 ft by the Kekoa camera, 400 ft higher than the evening's number; the morning update said about 5,100 ft, off by 500 ft; at 10:00, from the 09:00 base, about 4,900 ft, off by 700 ft. Most of the day the shear line was crossing Kula Highway near Omaopio; furthest north about 16:52, crossing Kula Highway near Kamehameha Schools. Data gaps: no readings all day from 1 station (Nakula); Kamehamenui 1 stopped at 14:48; Kula 1 stopped at 14:48; the Mesonet could not be reached on 9 of 53 updates.", "therm": "<strong>Light</strong> for the day, 10:00\u201314:00<div class=\"sub\">Kula Ag's measured air through the RRFS sounding (thermal.py); forecast was Moderate</div>", "base": "", "notes": ["Watched for: Late-day decay (P7) from 14:37.", "Camera against derived: morning about 200 ft higher, midday about 300 ft higher, afternoon about 500 ft higher."], "chart": "<div class=\"watch\"><div class=\"kind\">What the day did</div><ul><li>Watched for: Late-day decay (P7) from 14:37.</li><li>Camera against derived: morning about 200 ft higher, midday about 300 ft higher, afternoon about 500 ft higher.</li></ul></div><div style=\"font-weight:600;font-size:.9rem;margin:10px 0 2px\">Cloudbase</div><div style=\"display:flex;gap:14px;flex-wrap:wrap;font-size:.8rem;color:var(--muted,#6b6b66);margin:2px 0 4px\">\n<span><span style=\"display:inline-block;width:16px;border-top:2px dashed #eb6834;vertical-align:middle\"></span> Evening call + usual November day</span><span><span style=\"display:inline-block;width:16px;border-top:2px dashed #8a5cd6;vertical-align:middle\"></span> 10:00 + usual November day</span>\n<span><span style=\"display:inline-block;width:16px;height:2px;background:#2a78d6;vertical-align:middle\"></span> Derived (stations)</span><span><span style=\"display:inline-block;width:16px;height:2px;background:#3f9d5a;vertical-align:middle\"></span> Kekoa camera (1-hour median)</span><span><span style=\"display:inline-block;width:16px;border-top:2px dashed #3f9d5a;vertical-align:middle\"></span> Cumulus seen, no camera height yet (stations)</span><span><span style=\"display:inline-block;width:8px;height:8px;border-radius:50%;border:1.5px solid #898781;box-sizing:border-box;vertical-align:middle\"></span> Camera, no call</span></div>\n<div style=\"position:relative;width:100%;min-width:0;height:220px\"><canvas id=\"basechart\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Derived cloudbase against the forecast through the day\"></canvas></div>\n<div class=\"sub\">Derived from the stations every 15 minutes during the upslope. Lines: the evening call&#x27;s number and the 10:00 derived base, each carried along a usual November day (2024-26 history), drawn once and never redrawn.</div><details class=\"sub\" style=\"margin-top:6px\"><summary style=\"cursor:pointer\">How is the derived base worked out?</summary><div style=\"margin-top:6px;padding:8px 10px;border-left:3px solid var(--rule,#ddd)\"><p style=\"margin:0 0 6px\">Rising air cools about 5.4 &deg;F for every 1,000 ft it climbs, while its dew point drops only about 1 &deg;F. Where the two meet, the moisture condenses: that&rsquo;s the cloudbase. So a station&rsquo;s temperature and dew point tell how high its air would have to rise to make cloud: about 230 ft for every degree between them, added to the station&rsquo;s own height. 70 &deg;F with a 60 &deg;F dew point at Kula Ag (3,162 ft) gives about 5,400 ft.</p><p style=\"margin:0 0 6px\">The page does this for about a dozen slope stations every 15 minutes once the upslope has started, and shows the middle value.</p><p style=\"margin:0\">It can differ from the camera because the stations measure the air at the ground. Late in the day, or under cloud shade, that layer cools and moistens and no longer matches the air the thermals carry up, so the derived base reads low. Wet ground after dew or rain does the same in the morning. Before the upslope starts, the stations sit in the night&rsquo;s drainage air, so nothing is shown. When the camera has a reading, it leads.</p></div></details>\n<script>\n(function () {\n  var d = {\"derived\": [[540, 4270.0], [555, 4180.0], [570, 4290.0], [585, 4260.0], [600, 4390.0], [615, 4570.0], [630, 4780.0], [645, 4830.0], [660, 4930.0], [675, 4950.0], [690, 5100.0], [705, 5190.0], [720, 5300.0], [735, 5440.0], [750, 5500.0], [765, 5540.0], [780, 5370.0], [795, 5360.0], [810, 5370.0], [825, 5280.0], [840, 5220.0], [855, 5250.0], [870, 5420.0], [885, 5520.0], [900, 5480.0], [915, 5540.0], [930, 5560.0], [945, 5480.0], [960, 5370.0]], \"forecast\": [[540, 4970.0], [600, 5180.0], [660, 5300.0], [720, 5290.0], [780, 5140.0], [840, 5070.0], [900, 4890.0], [960, 4580.0]], \"camera\": [[593, 4520.0], [602, 4640.0], [611, 4730.0], [619, 4820.0], [628, 4960.0], [636, 5050.0], [645, 5080.0], [653, 5150.0], [662, 5200.0], [679, 5300.0], [688, 5450.0], [696, 5570.0], [705, 5570.0], [713, 5600.0], [722, 5640.0], [756, 5940.0], [773, 5670.0], [782, 5670.0], [791, 5620.0], [799, 5580.0], [808, 5540.0], [817, 5520.0], [825, 5520.0], [834, 5500.0], [842, 5500.0], [851, 5520.0], [868, 5540.0], [903, 6220.0], [912, 6220.0], [921, 6220.0]], \"camsub\": [[542, 4260.0], [555, 4260.0], [570, 4260.0], [585, 4380.0], [593, 4520.0]], \"hidden\": [], \"proj\": [[600, 4390.0], [660, 4510.0], [720, 4500.0], [780, 4350.0], [840, 4280.0], [900, 4100.0], [960, 3790.0]], \"nocall\": [576, 670, 730, 739, 748, 765, 859, 877, 894, 929, 938, 947, 956], \"up\": [540, 960], \"nocu\": null}, pt = function (a) { return {x: a[0], y: a[1]}; };\n  var dark = matchMedia('(prefers-color-scheme: dark)').matches, muted = '#898781', grid = dark ? '#2c2c2a' : '#e1e0d9';\n  var nocu = { id: 'nocu', beforeDatasetsDraw: function (c) { if (!d.nocu) return; var x = c.scales.x, a = c.chartArea, g = c.ctx,\n    x0 = x.getPixelForValue(d.nocu[0]), x1 = x.getPixelForValue(d.nocu[1]);\n    g.save(); g.fillStyle = 'rgba(137,135,129,0.10)'; g.fillRect(x0, a.top, x1 - x0, a.bottom - a.top);\n    g.fillStyle = muted; g.font = '11px sans-serif'; g.textAlign = 'center';\n    g.fillText('No cumulus', (x0 + x1) / 2, a.top + (a.bottom - a.top) / 2); g.restore(); } };\n  var band = { id: 'band', beforeDatasetsDraw: function (c) { if (!d.up) return; var x = c.scales.x, a = c.chartArea, g = c.ctx;\n    g.save(); g.fillStyle = 'rgba(137,135,129,0.14)';\n    g.fillRect(x.getPixelForValue(d.up[0]), a.top, x.getPixelForValue(d.up[1]) - x.getPixelForValue(d.up[0]), a.bottom - a.top); g.restore(); } };\n  // Landmarks on the slope (Sam, 10-31): dashed lines across the chart.\n  var marks = { id: 'marks', beforeDatasetsDraw: function (c) { var y = c.scales.y, a = c.chartArea, g = c.ctx;\n    [[4600, 'Treeline'], [6200, 'Ferns']].forEach(function (m) {\n      if (m[0] < y.min || m[0] > y.max) return; var py = y.getPixelForValue(m[0]);\n      g.save(); g.strokeStyle = muted; g.lineWidth = 1; g.setLineDash([4, 4]);\n      g.beginPath(); g.moveTo(a.left, py); g.lineTo(a.right, py); g.stroke();\n      g.setLineDash([]); g.fillStyle = muted; g.font = '11px sans-serif'; g.textAlign = 'right';\n      g.fillText(m[1], a.right - 4, py - 4); g.restore(); }); } };\n  var hm = function (m) { return String(Math.floor(m / 60)).padStart(2, '0') + ':' + String(m % 60).padStart(2, '0'); };\n  var ys = d.derived.map(function (a) { return a[1]; }).concat(d.forecast.map(function (a) { return a[1]; })).concat(d.camera.map(function (a) { return a[1]; })).concat(d.camsub.map(function (a) { return a[1]; })).concat(d.proj.map(function (a) { return a[1]; })).filter(function (v) { return v !== null; });\n  var xs = [540, 960];\n  var ymin = Math.min(3500, Math.floor(Math.min.apply(null, ys) / 500) * 500);\n  new Chart(document.getElementById('basechart'), {\n    type: 'line',\n    data: { datasets: [\n      { label: 'Derived', data: d.derived.map(pt), borderColor: '#2a78d6', borderWidth: 2, pointRadius: 0, tension: 0.3 },\n      { label: 'Forecast', data: d.forecast.map(pt), borderColor: '#eb6834', borderWidth: 2, borderDash: [6, 4], pointRadius: 3, pointBackgroundColor: '#eb6834', tension: 0.3 },\n      { label: 'Forecast (sounding)', data: d.proj.map(pt), borderColor: '#8a5cd6', borderWidth: 2, borderDash: [3, 4], pointRadius: 0, tension: 0.3 },\n      { label: 'Kekoa camera', data: d.camera.map(pt), borderColor: '#3f9d5a', borderWidth: 2, pointRadius: 0, tension: 0.3 },\n      { label: 'Cumulus seen, no camera height yet', data: d.camsub.map(pt), borderColor: '#3f9d5a', borderWidth: 2, borderDash: [5, 4], pointRadius: 0, tension: 0.3 },\n      { label: 'Camera hidden', data: d.hidden.map(function (m) { return {x: m, y: ymin}; }), showLine: false, clip: false,\n         pointRadius: 3, pointBackgroundColor: '#e0a100', borderColor: '#e0a100' },\n      { label: 'Camera, no call', data: d.nocall.map(function (m) { return {x: m, y: ymin}; }), showLine: false, clip: false,\n         pointRadius: 3, pointBorderWidth: 1.5, pointBackgroundColor: 'rgba(0,0,0,0)', borderColor: muted }\n    ] },\n    options: { responsive: true, maintainAspectRatio: false, interaction: { mode: 'nearest', axis: 'x', intersect: false },\n      plugins: { legend: { display: false }, tooltip: { callbacks: {\n        title: function (i) { return hm(i[0].parsed.x); },\n        label: function (i) { return i.dataset.label === 'Camera hidden' ? 'Camera hidden: cloud or rain at the camera'\n          : i.dataset.label === 'Camera, no call' ? 'Camera: no call'\n          : i.dataset.label + ': ' + Math.round(i.parsed.y).toLocaleString() + ' ft'; } } } },\n      scales: {\n        x: { type: 'linear', min: xs[0], max: xs[1], ticks: { stepSize: 60, color: muted, callback: function (v) { return hm(v); } }, grid: { display: false } },\n        y: { min: ymin,\n              max: Math.max(7000, Math.ceil(Math.max.apply(null, ys) / 500) * 500),\n              ticks: { stepSize: 500, color: muted, callback: function (v) { return v.toLocaleString(); } }, grid: { color: grid } }\n      } },\n    plugins: [nocu, marks]\n  });\n})();\n</script>", "line": "Crossing Kula Highway near Omaopio<div class=\"sub\">Most of the day, 34 updates</div>", "up": "<span class=\"num\">09:00</span> to about <span class=\"num\">17:00</span>", "wind": "<span class=\"num\">4 mph</span>, gusts to 13<div class=\"sub\">Lower elevations, during the upslope</div>"}